[stderr] # Canonical specification index
[stderr] 
[stderr] This directory is the canonical, resumable specification for **mock-fantasy-quest-4**. It consolidates F001–F010 without overriding [`INITIAL.md`](../INITIAL.md), which remains the source of truth. A later author must cite stable IDs here rather than rediscovering scope.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Control rules
[stderr] 
[stderr] - **P0** is an original, offline-capable 2D single-player fantasy RPG: one town, one dungeon, a short guided campaign and ending, exploration, dialogue/quests, party turn combat, inventory, local saves/recovery, settings/accessibility, responsive web, and PWA distribution.
[stderr] - Target-neutral rules live in `requirements.*`; the web/PWA differences live in `platform-appendix.md`. PWA is a delivery adaptation of the shared game, not a second game.
[stderr] - `Final Fantasy V` is a functional scope reference for party-based turn adventure only. It permits no copied expression: names, lore, text, art, music, maps, layouts, UI flows, or interaction choreography.
[stderr] - `proposed` requirements and every `GATE-*` are not implementation authorisation. Resolve their linked `DEC-*` record before allocating dependent work.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Chapter register
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Chapter ID | Document / owner | Depends on | State |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | SPEC-00 | `00-domain-discovery.md` / product discovery | INITIAL | complete |
[stderr] | SPEC-01 | `01-product-brief.md` / product | SPEC-00 | complete |
[stderr] | SPEC-02 | `02-feature-model.md` / game design | SPEC-00–01 | complete |
[stderr] | SPEC-03 | `03-technical-contract.md` / technical design | SPEC-00–02 | complete |
[stderr] | SPEC-04 | `04-experience-contract.md` / experience design | SPEC-00–03 | complete |
[stderr] | SPEC-11 | `requirements.md`, `requirements.json` / F011 specification owner | SPEC-00–04, planning 05–10 | complete |
[stderr] | SPEC-12 | `traceability-matrix.md` / F011 specification owner | SPEC-11 | complete; runbook IDs pending F012+ |
[stderr] | SPEC-13 | `decision-log.md` / product owner | SPEC-00–04 | open decisions recorded |
[stderr] | SPEC-14 | `platform-appendix.md` / technical + experience owner | SPEC-11 | complete; thresholds gated |
[stderr] | SPEC-15 | `domain-completeness-review.md` / F011 specification owner | SPEC-00–04, SPEC-11 | complete; gated domains retained |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Bounded expansion protocol
[stderr] 
[stderr] Expand one domain chapter at a time, preserving IDs and this register: identify entities/rules, authoring inputs, dependencies, P0 boundary, target adaptations, verification, and open decisions. Proposed detailed chapters are shell/session, campaign content, combat, progression/inventory, persistence/recovery, experience/accessibility, PWA/release, and connected-scope holds. A chapter can move from `planned` to `complete` only when its requirements, trace rows, and decision/risk links exist; it never closes a human gate.
[stderr] # Supervisor — evidence-gated LangGraph task orchestration
[stderr] 
[stderr] This package orchestrates one small, reviewable runbook task at a time. It
[stderr] does not impose an application stack, model provider, or QA workflow. Each
[stderr] project's versioned root `.env` is the source of truth for its repository
[stderr] path, enabled agents, execution order, worker commands, validation commands,
[stderr] timeouts, publishing policy, observability, and platform-specific tooling.
[stderr] Supervisor provides evidence-gated orchestration around that project contract.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Quick start
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### Install the Supervisor CLI
[stderr] 
[stderr] Download the installer, review it if desired, then run it. It installs into
[stderr] `~/.local/share/supervisor` and links the commands into `~/.local/bin` without
[stderr] requiring administrator access:
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```zsh
[stderr] curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jakowicz/supervisor/main/scripts/install.sh -o /tmp/supervisor-install.sh
[stderr] bash /tmp/supervisor-install.sh
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] If `~/.local/bin` is not already on your `PATH`, the installer prints the one
[stderr] `export PATH=...` line to add to your shell profile. Set
[stderr] `SUPERVISOR_PYTHON=/path/to/python` only when you need to override its automatic
[stderr] Python 3.10+ selection.
[stderr] 
[stderr] To update the global/installed CLI itself, run:
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```zsh
[stderr] supervisor upgrade
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] To update the Supervisor checkout inside the project you are working in, run
[stderr] this from that project directory (or one of its subdirectories):
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```zsh
[stderr] supervisor update
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] It finds the nearest `supervisor/` checkout, fast-forwards it, and reinstalls
[stderr] that project's commands into its virtual environment. It refuses to update when
[stderr] that checkout has local edits, so it cannot overwrite work. Commit the resulting
[stderr] submodule-pointer change in the parent project when you are happy with it.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### New project
[stderr] 
[stderr] From an existing Supervisor installation, create a ready-to-configure project:
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```zsh
[stderr] supervisor init
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] The first question asks for the new project directory; enter the location you
[stderr] want to initialise. You may still pass that directory as an optional argument
[stderr] when convenient.
[stderr] 
[stderr] `init` automatically selects a compatible Python 3.10+ interpreter from your
[stderr] `PATH`, then creates a Git repository, adds this repository as `supervisor/`, creates
[stderr] `runbooks/TEMPLATE.md`, creates versioned root `.env` configuration plus ignored
[stderr] root `.secrets.env` credentials, and installs the local virtual environment. It is interactive: it asks for the
[stderr] initial shared-Langfuse account only when no local service is running, then
[stderr] prompts for this project's worker commands/models, retry policy, Git policy,
[stderr] dashboard preference, and Langfuse project credentials. It reuses the one
[stderr] shared Langfuse service at `http://127.0.0.1:3001` when it is already running.
[stderr] Use `--non-interactive` only for automated provisioning.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Every setup prompt shows a safe default where one exists. The selected project
[stderr] profile is only a starting point: inspect and change the generated `.env` to
[stderr] choose the agents, stage order, validation commands, models, browser/visual QA,
[stderr] and publishing policy appropriate to that project.
[stderr] 
[stderr] When configuration needs Langfuse project keys, Supervisor first checks the
[stderr] shared local service. If it is not running, it asks permission to start the
[stderr] one shared local stack, clearly states that it is installing/starting Langfuse,
[stderr] and asks for the initial administrator username (email), display name, and
[stderr] password. That bootstrap creates the default project and securely registers
[stderr] its key pair for later project setups. If the service is already
[stderr] running, Supervisor reuses those registered keys when available. Langfuse OSS
[stderr] does not provide the organization-level project-provisioning API required to
[stderr] automatically create another project on a running instance, so a project with
[stderr] unknown credentials still prompts for its existing key pair rather than
[stderr] modifying the service database.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### Existing project
[stderr] 
[stderr] Add the Supervisor as a submodule, install it, then configure the project:
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```zsh
[stderr] git submodule add git@github.com:jakowicz/supervisor.git supervisor
[stderr] cd supervisor
[stderr] python3.11 -m venv .venv
[stderr] ./.venv/bin/python -m pip install -e '.[dev]'
[stderr] ./.venv/bin/supervisor configure
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### Run your first task
[stderr] 
[stderr] Create a small runbook from `../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md`, for example
[stderr] `../runbooks/T001.md`. In the project-root `.env`, configure the workers you intend
[stderr] to use and explicitly allow edits. Then run the task and inspect its report:
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```zsh
[stderr] ./.venv/bin/supervisor-run --runbook ../runbooks/T001.md
[stderr] ./.venv/bin/supervisor-reports browse
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] Evidence, SQLite history, checkpoints, reports, and raw logs always live under
[stderr] the controlled project's `.state/` directory—not inside `supervisor/`.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Prerequisites
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Python 3.10 or newer (the current machine's Python 3.9.6 is too old)
[stderr] - The executables named by your project's `.env` validation and worker commands
[stderr] - Node/npm and a browser only when the configured browser QA command needs them
[stderr] - A game profile starts with Flutter validation commands; non-game projects do
[stderr]   not require Flutter unless they configure it
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Setup
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```bash
[stderr] cd supervisor
[stderr] python3.11 -m venv .venv
[stderr] source .venv/bin/activate
[stderr] pip install -e '.[dev]'
[stderr] cp .env.example ../.env
[stderr] cp .secrets.env.example ../.secrets.env
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Configuration and credentials
[stderr] 
[stderr] Supervisor reads two files from the project root, in this order:
[stderr] 
[stderr] | File | Commit it? | Purpose |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | `.env` | Yes | Non-secret project contract: agents, commands, tests, models, retry limits, publishing, observability, asset settings, and paths. |
[stderr] | `.secrets.env` | No | Credentials only, such as API keys and Langfuse keys. Values here override values from `.env`. |
[stderr] | `.secrets.env.example` | Yes | Empty, documented template showing which credential keys may be supplied. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] Never put credentials in `.env`. Keep `.secrets.env` out of Git and restrict it
[stderr] to the people and automation that need access.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Run `supervisor configure` after `supervisor init`, after adding Supervisor to
[stderr] an existing project, or whenever the project's agents, validation, models,
[stderr] publishing policy, or observability setup changes. It updates the project-root
[stderr] `.env` and writes any credentials it collects to `.secrets.env`; it does not
[stderr] print secret values. Re-run it safely to revise the project contract:
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```zsh
[stderr] supervisor configure
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] Use `supervisor update` to apply safe, versioned additions to `.env` supplied
[stderr] by newer Supervisor releases. It preserves project choices and never writes
[stderr] credentials into `.env`.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### Start a new project
[stderr] 
[stderr] From any existing supervisor installation, create an empty project with the
[stderr] supervisor checked out as a `supervisor/` Git submodule, a root `runbooks/`
[stderr] directory, a starter runbook, versioned configuration, a private ignored
[stderr] `.secrets.env` credential file, and an installed virtual environment:
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```zsh
[stderr] supervisor init
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] The command first asks for the new project directory, refuses a non-empty
[stderr] destination, and never overwrites an existing project. It also reuses the shared local Langfuse service at
[stderr] `http://127.0.0.1:3001`; only when that endpoint is absent does it run the
[stderr] local observability bootstrap. It uses `git@github.com:jakowicz/supervisor.git` by default; use
[stderr] `--supervisor-url <URL>` to select a fork or another remote. Use `--no-install`
[stderr] when creating the virtual environment and dependencies is not currently
[stderr] possible, or `--no-observability` when configuring a remote/shared service
[stderr] yourself, then complete the install later from `<project>/supervisor`:
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```zsh
[stderr] python3.11 -m venv .venv
[stderr] ./.venv/bin/python -m pip install -e '.[dev]'
[stderr] ./.venv/bin/supervisor configure
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] Runtime evidence is deliberately stored at `<project>/.state/`; no operational
[stderr] `.state/` directory is created inside the reusable `supervisor/` submodule.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Set `SUPERVISOR_REPO_ROOT` to the controlled project root if invoking from
[stderr] another directory. Add worker command adapters only after verifying their
[stderr] credentials, permissions, and worktree handling.
[stderr] 
[stderr] For a reusable project setup, run the interactive configuration CLI after the
[stderr] editable install:
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```bash
[stderr] supervisor configure
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] It writes versioned project-root `.env` configuration and keeps credentials in
[stderr] ignored, mode-600 `.secrets.env`; it prompts for project paths, enabled agents
[stderr] and their commands/models, total retry attempts, dashboard preference, Git
[stderr] policy, timeouts, and optional Langfuse credentials. The dashboard chooses
