[stderr] authorisation is recorded; do not turn a gate into approval.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Required behaviour
[stderr] 
[stderr] Select no more than one queued chapter whose dependencies and gates permit
[stderr] planning. Add at most 250 stable `IMP-*` contracts with requirement links,
[stderr] owned files/data/interfaces, dependencies, non-goals, platform distinctions,
[stderr] verification, asset assessment, and canonical source links. Validate coverage,
[stderr] unique IDs, ownership, and acyclic dependencies. Allocate only ready
[stderr] unassigned contracts, using monotonic B/R counters and batches of no more than
[stderr] seven R IDs; materialise at most ten corresponding B runbooks. Each B writer
[stderr] must contain a context packet, output list, validation procedure,
[stderr] checkpoint/update procedure, collision stop rule, and stop condition. Do not
[stderr] create R-series files yourself.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Checkpoint and update procedure
[stderr] 
[stderr] Atomically update the JSON/Markdown ledger counters, chapter state, contract
[stderr] allocations, and checkpoint after validation. Never renumber, replace, or
[stderr] rewrite an accepted B/R contract. If work remains, create exactly one new
[stderr] dispatcher with the next monotonic dispatcher ID and a later sequence. If no
[stderr] queued chapter or ready contract remains, create exactly one final audit
[stderr] B-series runbook that validates all completed catalogue expansions and batches;
[stderr] it must not pretend to generate or review all work in this dispatch.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Validation procedure
[stderr] 
[stderr] Validate JSON, the 250-contract chapter cap, no more than ten newly-created B
