[stderr] ## Objective
[stderr] 
[stderr] Create only `../runbooks/R0001.md` from manifest batch B0001. Its precise
[stderr] contract is IMP-0001, "Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline". It is
[stderr] not permission to implement the game or resolve GATE-0001.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Context packet
[stderr] 
[stderr] Read `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition`,
[stderr] `../specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability`,
[stderr] `../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json` (IMP-0001), and the B0001/R0001
[stderr] manifest records. Use `../../../runbooks/TEMPLATE.md` for the Supervisor shape.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Output list
[stderr] 
[stderr] - `../runbooks/R0001.md` only; metadata must use `task_id: R0001`, `sequence: 1`, `source_catalogue_ids: IMP-0001`, `authoring_batch: B0001`, `factory_stages: F011,F012,F013`, and the manifest provenance/asset values.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Required authoring content
[stderr] 
[stderr] Give R0001 a small, precise objective; dependencies; relevant requirement IDs;
[stderr] owned files, data, and interfaces; required behaviour; non-goals; web/PWA
[stderr] platform differences; verification commands and evidence; observable acceptance
[stderr] criteria; and an `## Asset assessment` explaining that no asset is needed and
[stderr] incidental asset creation is prohibited. Include all required standard front
[stderr] matter, including `asset_impact: not_applicable`, blank `asset_ids`, and the
[stderr] non-empty provenance fields exactly as the manifest records them.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Validation procedure
[stderr] 
[stderr] Before writing, stop if R0001 exists with a different ID, catalogue mapping,
[stderr] provenance, dependency set, or output owner. After writing, load it with
[stderr] `supervisor.runbooks.load_task`, compare every metadata value and dependency
[stderr] against the manifest, and confirm it has all required sections.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Checkpoint and update procedure
[stderr] 
[stderr] Update only B0001's manifest state/checkpoint after successful validation.
[stderr] Retain R0001 and its ID on any failure; repair that one path on resume.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Stop condition
[stderr] 
[stderr] Stop after R0001. Do not create another R file, choose a framework, or pass GATE-0001.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Exactly one R-series runbook, R0001, is created for the allocated IMP-0001 contract.
[stderr] - R0001 is a bounded implementation task with the required sections, metadata, provenance, and explicit no-asset assessment.
